// Build configuration for `npm run build` (§G11 "Build").
//
// It extends tsconfig.json and changes only what blocks emit:
//
//   * `noEmit: false` + `outDir` — the base config is a check-only config.
//   * `allowImportingTsExtensions: false` — the base config turns it on because
//     `npm test` runs TypeScript sources directly through
//     `node --experimental-strip-types`, and TypeScript rejects that flag
//     together with emit. Sources that will ship must import specifiers that
//     resolve after compilation; `src/graph-client.ts` has no imports at all,
//     so nothing needs rewriting today.
//   * `exclude` — `*.test.ts` files are the test surface, not plugin output.
//
// No bundler is configured on purpose. docs/development-guide.md §G2 leaves the
// EmDash sandbox runtime unresolved and §15 has not approved a bundler
// dependency, so `emdash-plugin bundle` (or whatever Phase 0 confirms) owns
// bundling; this script only produces the compiled module graph.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": false,
    "outDir": "dist",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": false
  },
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts"]
}
